      },
      "narration_text": "Here's the problem. A meeting ends, everyone nods, and a week later nothing moved. And the easy A I move — ask it to summarize — gives you a tidy paragraph that nobody owns. So here's the frame that fixes it. A real action item is three things: an owner, a task, and a due date. You triage them by priority — impact plus urgency. And the rule that does the work: if it has no owner or no date, it is not an action yet.",
